DESCRIPTION:Earth Day falls on April 22 and began as one day of American pr
 otest in 1970\, proposed by Senator Gaylord Nelson of Wisconsin and organi
 zed in about six months. The U.S. Senate's own history puts the turnout at
  roughly 20 million people\, across some 2\,000 college campuses and 10\,0
 00 schools\, though no source names who counted. It has been international
  since 1990\, and it has never been a federal holiday.\n\nhttps://todaycel
 ebrates.com/holiday/earth-day/
